      "message": "Well it\u0027s adding complexity to an already well obfuscated piece of code.\n\nSo the difference between your 2 clauses is:\n#define CONFIG_RW_SIG_ADDR (CONFIG_PROGRAM_MEMORY_BASE  + CONFIG_RW_MEM_OFF + CONFIG_RW_SIZE - CONFIG_RW_SIG_SIZE)\nvs\n#define CONFIG_RW_SIG_ADDR (CONFIG_PROGRAM_MEMORY_BASE  + CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE                                         - CONFIG_RW_SIG_SIZE)\n\nThus:\nCONFIG_RW_MEM_OFF + CONFIG_RW_SIZE vs CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE \n\nIf I try to resolve the former:\nCONFIG_RW_MEM_OFF + CONFIG_RW_SIZE \u003d\nCONFIG_SHAREDLIB_MEM_OFF +  CONFIG_SHAREDLIB_SIZE + _IMAGE_SIZE \u003d\nCONFIG_RO_MEM_OFF +  _IMAGE_SIZE +  CONFIG_SHAREDLIB_SIZE + _IMAGE_SIZE \u003d\nCONFIG_RO_MEM_OFF +  CONFIG_SHAREDLIB_SIZE +  (CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE -  CONFIG_SHAREDLIB_SIZE) \u003d\nCONFIG_RO_MEM_OFF + CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE  \n\nSo   CONFIG_RO_MEM_OFF + CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE  vs CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE \nThe one you added is more correct.\nAnd both are equals in all exisiting cases in the code base.\n\nI would just keep the new one.\n\n\nFor RO, I think the net difference is :\n CONFIG_RO_MEM_OFF   -   CONFIG_SHAREDLIB_SIZE/2 + CONFIG_FW_PSTATE_SIZE\n\nSame thing for CONFIG_RO_MEM_OFF , that\u0027s a \u0027bug\u0027 in the former implementation (well actually a bug when the correct implementation was \u0027cleaned-up\u0027 ...)\nFor the CONFIG_SHAREDLIB_SIZE, I would argue it\u0027s a bug in your new implementation (overall it doesn\u0027t exist anywhere, that\u0027s kind of a silly moot debate ... and the \u0027/2\u0027 might be a bug here ???)\nFor  CONFIG_FW_PSTATE_SIZE, I imagine that\u0027s the only detail this CL is trying to solve,\nmaybe it would be nice to see it clearly in the #if/#else.",
